 ## Subtopics
 
+### ViiNeuS
+A hybrid implicit surface learning method that efficiently initializes the signed distance field (SDF) to reconstruct large driving scenes from 2D street view images with limited overlap, without relying on geometric priors or LiDAR [S1, unofficial].
+
 ### Polygonal Mesh Sampling and Octahedral Initialization
-This variant addresses slow and unstable convergence on tilted surfaces by replacing standard cube-based sampling with polygonal meshes [S3]. It initializes a 128×128×128 grid, selecting the center point of each grid along with its six neighboring grids (front, back, left, right, top, and bottom) to create polygonal meshes [S3]. To further improve convergence, it utilizes a regular octahedron with 20 faces (8 exterior, 12 interior) instead of standard cubes [S3]. The ray from camera origin to pixel is defined as $r(t) = o + td$, where $d = (\theta, \phi)$ is the viewing direction. The intersection of this ray with the polygonal meshes serves as the sampling point [S3]. Unlike standard NeRF, this method predicts opacity $\alpha$ directly instead of volume density, using the rendering equation $\hat{C}(r) = \sum_{i=1}^{N} T_i \alpha_i c_i$, where $T_i = \prod_{j=0}^{i-1} (1 - \alpha_j)$ [S3].
