 ### NeRF-DS
-NeRF-DS extends NeRF to capture dynamic, reflective objects [S4]. It employs a dual-network design similar to D-NeRF: a deformation field maps time-varying coordinates into a canonical space [S4]. It uses a specularity-aware radiance field that jointly predicts view-dependent appearance and reflection behavior, conditioning radiance on surface orientation and spatial location. An object mask is used to maintain temporal consistency under changing reflections [S4].
